bove shows the relationship between the grades obtained in science and literature tests among a particular group of students.\nWhich of the following is the trend line of the scatter plot above?" :question/worked-solution "From the plot, it seems that the data points are scattered randomly. Therefore, there is no linear trend." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134006/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "327d9a77-b2dd-57b1-b959-570684714bf9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134006"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134023/selection/97ebb5126bb493225151010253aebffc44cd3819fb1c950e856f834fd2af38fe" :answer/id #uuid "5700f2a2-25ac-520b-b009-f748c7211115" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{8}{5}x-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134023/selection/759382e512e0f3adfc4d540e5d44e8b6037425bf25577f83a78d9cee4fd22fb8" :answer/id #uuid "99ff009d-84f3-52e2-9e75-d2c333669fc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134023/selection/67adde7d2979e9b8aa168ec09e7defe19b8b36fbc355b2340d8b2d24da22d3dd" :answer/id #uuid "7e78102d-ff88-586b-ba3a-50c68ff0b439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134023/selection/f26f341edea8bc931ab63ee2b780baca1520e94940b15357be42b5905ab04df2" :answer/id #uuid "5d19758b-bd47-52c6-a3a4-0ac4db2868c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{5}x-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134023/selection/b575d215823202e32076eb7f93ed34bc2f895259bc157645c3300b891b1cdfad" :answer/id #uuid "138dc2ad-1379-5fa1-837a-4735ef7fc21f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134023/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1abdaa-816d-5b68-a847-d70b8dee2562" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134023/selection/b575d215823202e32076eb7f93ed34bc2f895259bc157645c3300b891b1cdfad" :answer-field/choices ["q-134023/selection/97ebb5126bb493225151010253aebffc44cd3819fb1c950e856f834fd2af38fe" "q-134023/selection/759382e512e0f3adfc4d540e5d44e8b6037425bf25577f83a78d9cee4fd22fb8" "q-134023/selection/67adde7d2979e9b8aa168ec09e7defe19b8b36fbc355b2340d8b2d24da22d3dd" "q-134023/selection/f26f341edea8bc931ab63ee2b780baca1520e94940b15357be42b5905ab04df2" "q-134023/selection/b575d215823202e32076eb7f93ed34bc2f895259bc157645c3300b891b1cdfad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134023" :question/id #uuid "e2360671-96ab-5521-825d-76752c839c61" :question/math-academy-id "q-134023" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/1c9f30692222eaaed4cda6b608dcc1ccb01eefd6b5fa7730b5b8bb29c9f528b1.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(7,8).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-2}{7-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=\\frac{6}{5}$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{6}{5}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{6}{5}x+b \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{6}{5}(2)+b \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{12}{5}+b \\\\ 10 & =12+5b \\\\ -2 & =5b \\\\ b & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134023/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134023"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-133765"] :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(4,1)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(8,9).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-1}{8-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-134019/selection/e83936b2040e990c675676615cc08f28d619267d7540ba9ffb088808b5b24422" :answer/id #uuid "70379917-c5bd-5434-8cbc-f3d8ee725056" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{7}x+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134019/selection/5751eafe9d8091bf30478401b8394990600555de1e67b61be575f20ae54ab5dd" :answer/id #uuid "271c1441-92dd-5749-a225-2cc308cdca1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{6}{7}x+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134019/selection/23bacef1a366dec0a104682fb68c5beded40c5266925b1ba0adda5dc7f065ab9" :answer/id #uuid "dca10fd8-90c8-5c9f-991c-b72c852548ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{7}x+8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134019/selection/dc556b444b9dedb08348946a3888b0f43a654c73efbfd4e17b69a8453198e219" :answer/id #uuid "dd475ef0-8f46-580c-9077-d17e7f8758b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{6}{7}x+8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134019/selection/5b4601d936d0858cb6201c0fc4eecc34273c4d1250518475d57df4847fdeb41e" :answer/id #uuid "ba58e62d-472c-5500-97ca-e724a8e2c73e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{2}{3}x+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134019/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "baa20bd2-7fc3-54ff-a621-afe065059849" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134019/selection/5751eafe9d8091bf30478401b8394990600555de1e67b61be575f20ae54ab5dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-134019/selection/e83936b2040e990c675676615cc08f28d619267d7540ba9ffb088808b5b24422" "q-134019/selection/5751eafe9d8091bf30478401b8394990600555de1e67b61be575f20ae54ab5dd" "q-134019/selection/23bacef1a366dec0a104682fb68c5beded40c5266925b1ba0adda5dc7f065ab9" "q-134019/selection/dc556b444b9dedb08348946a3888b0f43a654c73efbfd4e17b69a8453198e219" "q-134019/selection/5b4601d936d0858cb6201c0fc4eecc34273c4d1250518475d57df4847fdeb41e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134019" :question/id #uuid "0fd50200-c5bb-57f9-8883-bf1a29b8fe86" :question/math-academy-id "q-134019" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/31394106551498e7fd3a5cf57773f11ae31c7bc80c9a12272e95033bdcfd462e.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,9)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(7,3).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-9}{7-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{7} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-\\frac{6}{7}$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{6}{7}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(0,9):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{6}{7}x+b \\\\ 9 & =-\\frac{6}{7}(0)+b \\\\ 9 & =0+b \\\\ b & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{6}{7}x+9.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134019/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134019"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134011/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "b36fd1f5-35cc-5130-89f6-70d53c09aee5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134011/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "91dde2eb-3289-51bb-9c33-f6f018b32382" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134011/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "4d66408e-62f4-5062-9348-7155371034f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134011/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "c11cafbc-eb70-5192-bbcf-20f8657e0ccb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134011/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "1ce2c447-97b7-5668-af9a-b235a4eea186" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134011/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "33b96466-10f7-5a39-98a1-d4a885f0cf31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134011/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer-field/choices ["q-134011/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-134011/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-134011/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-134011/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-134011/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134011" :question/id #uuid "9c657514-3c46-5f1c-8175-539557f1e6c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-134011" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/c55d326b26a8bb6831f38456b7b47878ef66a185090c7327cbb151c4e951be33.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(3,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(5,1).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2}{5-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134011/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134011"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134013/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "0a46f265-1ccc-5848-a747-f5fe26d3c062" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134013/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "b52e5e66-fe54-5898-ba03-5acce5527ef5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134013/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "d97299a8-aa3c-52d4-9f77-de53c2a9e05d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134013/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "33abcfc9-59c6-5387-9d91-b39a3e79a16b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134013/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "62ff1108-b47a-5bd8-825f-b4d7c9f2fcd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134013/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5054ba7a-37e1-55ef-ba37-624f690540b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134013/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer-field/choices ["q-134013/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-134013/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-134013/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" "q-134013/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-134013/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134013" :question/id #uuid "8fc30479-0ae1-5397-a71e-95530d9018e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-134013" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/72a4541fa9349de3a1d7218f3622ebb7536cc460bbf32fd90e43c754fac909a3.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,-1)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(3,1).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-1)}{3-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134013/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134013"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134031/selection/f535c223daac49a538e12c4d9bdbbe1a4d0636a086b26be5292cb6de7153dc80" :answer/id #uuid "147cb5c3-b855-5a29-9c61-313f0722e002" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-0.5x+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134031/selection/acb44b75765b7952ae05d89770fb847b52d1066a206096e628e303a1320e868d" :answer/id #uuid "9b0beaf6-32cc-5017-a4e5-fba2ab01c6c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1.5x+6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134031/selection/e246286508fee4d57bb91094fb18afaa459b450ac15a1bd77d446ffd4001097b" :answer/id #uuid "9c14989c-504d-54b8-82ae-adbda82b673f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-0.5x+7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134031/selection/cd1a91a83421c7e91170eb14429443f6e7056a7b994e603b467fb2c2420703be" :answer/id #uuid "28a165f6-3fa0-5290-ad54-1faf12b0de17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-x+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134031/selection/23532bb0dc7f8943f7196a206ea57bf35c9adb93eac215f9686fc89b2c293efd" :answer/id #uuid "96aa7826-18c7-5233-a1af-61234fa47138" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-x+7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134031/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7633dab5-aa8e-57f3-83d2-6313382bf24d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134031/selection/23532bb0dc7f8943f7196a206ea57bf35c9adb93eac215f9686fc89b2c293efd" :answer-field/choices ["q-134031/selection/f535c223daac49a538e12c4d9bdbbe1a4d0636a086b26be5292cb6de7153dc80" "q-134031/selection/acb44b75765b7952ae05d89770fb847b52d1066a206096e628e303a1320e868d" "q-134031/selection/e246286508fee4d57bb91094fb18afaa459b450ac15a1bd77d446ffd4001097b" "q-134031/selection/cd1a91a83421c7e91170eb14429443f6e7056a7b994e603b467fb2c2420703be" "q-134031/selection/23532bb0dc7f8943f7196a206ea57bf35c9adb93eac215f9686fc89b2c293efd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134031" :question/id #uuid "4ea3c63e-d2ec-56ec-acdc-942ec91b6a05" :question/math-academy-id "q-134031" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/111833881cf8e939d896f23a5ab7ca436f9265e7b8fd66c099eb118eab8fd6b0.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/fdad2c939372e14617ba4e393037d7f5852cd8114467aa914ccb8963c0eacfeb.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(2,5)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(6,1).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-5}{6-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{4} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-1$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-x+b \\\\ 5 & =-2+b \\\\ 7 & =b \\\\ b & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-x+7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134031/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134031"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134033/selection/749eb139fdbd121b73fa3a799a4c3ef1b44fea50910782d98f7a21b6fbe9aa6f" :answer/id #uuid "30bb6390-7c3b-5f68-b4c4-4d709f90c81a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-0.5x+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134033/selection/a6641636872c672f55faf0efd1738f2be06aba636809c9655a6cfc4a8fb8f888" :answer/id #uuid "1b64ef8d-69a2-5d6b-b9de-a75b9f706368" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-x+10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134033/selection/347e63bb4a291fdccf3f0a7943ee12da861e9872ada7f5a644d4e2cbe07f8d22" :answer/id #uuid "ec7b281b-c060-5115-ba7f-5f12a298bed9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3x+12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134033/selection/8f60e48f1b7fb3d0ba1bc0a032ef75fb05a4eb99b8d5383bc65366b2924719ff" :answer/id #uuid "d7452534-b1e2-5615-9ed3-a9436967e6f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-x+12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134033/selection/c51f2ae4976dcdec39101692016f1bcc4b95aa7d61504adcfc897c147fb2d483" :answer/id #uuid "509f7578-fc59-56b3-803f-671282d51c22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2x+10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134033/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c24bdab6-a9a1-505c-8c97-8126c5747911" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134033/selection/c51f2ae4976dcdec39101692016f1bcc4b95aa7d61504adcfc897c147fb2d483" :answer-field/choices ["q-134033/selection/749eb139fdbd121b73fa3a799a4c3ef1b44fea50910782d98f7a21b6fbe9aa6f" "q-134033/selection/a6641636872c672f55faf0efd1738f2be06aba636809c9655a6cfc4a8fb8f888" "q-134033/selection/347e63bb4a291fdccf3f0a7943ee12da861e9872ada7f5a644d4e2cbe07f8d22" "q-134033/selection/8f60e48f1b7fb3d0ba1bc0a032ef75fb05a4eb99b8d5383bc65366b2924719ff" "q-134033/selection/c51f2ae4976dcdec39101692016f1bcc4b95aa7d61504adcfc897c147fb2d483"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134033" :question/id #uuid "f5c3f41a-a5ad-5dad-b06b-1fd6da917e30" :question/math-academy-id "q-134033" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/24d3507598aa125a515534fd79c82e051875e897bedbe333cdaaf4e4856f67e4.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/f62fe2cf8d93e0737482334a6f659202032160d451e6518afa152f43fb51d0a7.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(2,6)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(4,2).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-6}{4-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{2} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-2$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-2x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+b \\\\ 6 & =-2(2)+b \\\\ 6 & =-4+b \\\\ 10 & =b \\\\ b & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-2x+10.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134033/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134033"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-133768"] :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/0575edf80f4a6f26c8f1002404ac04331d4c5d1f81b644021bc6284a6212338a.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(2,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(6,8).$\n\nTherefore, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-2}{6-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-134032/selection/79a626ff1681542e1d4cd976c0429023f481a9f5127def3e8ed36a5fea930eda" :answer/id #uuid "3092f54f-8f8e-5170-9c74-8f3e84b72cfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1.5x-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134032/selection/d5df5356693bd103f7bc4ab1b464383fe0f01fbe3b09a80add3d304866bc4b9c" :answer/id #uuid "6bc4f3b7-26e4-5df3-b655-917928c75092" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1.5x-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134032/selection/a21080f7f1635d2b52f40beee6d7b8038154167545cba2ae63aaef28b5394db3" :answer/id #uuid "fa193485-8256-58f9-9c4b-55f4f697ef67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134032/selection/2f8b0b7762735e41436c78ba4de49f8c56363de87df782b30d2dcf90f7f66465" :answer/id #uuid "df756c2b-c704-5ad5-9a24-ec07cdf51a7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2.5x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134032/selection/0db32750223419c0445a3c8e2f10be0ab1fbdae0b1da1e58b3d34a193fa0c9f3" :answer/id #uuid "0c4da729-75ff-5299-af69-9e8ac36242a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134032/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ede40fa3-2a42-5d3c-a69c-3f29eebcee88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134032/selection/a21080f7f1635d2b52f40beee6d7b8038154167545cba2ae63aaef28b5394db3" :answer-field/choices ["q-134032/selection/79a626ff1681542e1d4cd976c0429023f481a9f5127def3e8ed36a5fea930eda" "q-134032/selection/d5df5356693bd103f7bc4ab1b464383fe0f01fbe3b09a80add3d304866bc4b9c" "q-134032/selection/a21080f7f1635d2b52f40beee6d7b8038154167545cba2ae63aaef28b5394db3" "q-134032/selection/2f8b0b7762735e41436c78ba4de49f8c56363de87df782b30d2dcf90f7f66465" "q-134032/selection/0db32750223419c0445a3c8e2f10be0ab1fbdae0b1da1e58b3d34a193fa0c9f3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134032" :question/id #uuid "7c5f022b-dc24-5d6e-9e31-83f3aaacf0d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-134032" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/d23d6a35343aebcb986118bd7c5bc720f00480706057ec900e55c75bac296ebb.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/663e4d77d51816641a9fa861f37893d9f986d5e2b00e605ed5eb4fc19d40eab4.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(5,5)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(7,9).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-5}{7-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=2$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=2x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(5,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x+b \\\\ 5 & =2(5)+b \\\\ 5 & =10+b \\\\ -5 & =b \\\\ b & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=2x-5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134032/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134032"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-133769"] :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/fd3ce3de75fa9296c721e3f3a28bef241eae6350819c4cc7a54707921c0c1fe4.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(2,7)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(8,4).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-7}{8-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{6} \\\\  & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-0.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-0.5x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,7):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.5x+b \\\\ 7 & =-0.5(2)+b \\\\ 7 & =-1+b \\\\ 8 & =b \\\\ b & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-0.5x+8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
